## Volume Pricing System

### Configuration Structure

- **Global Settings**: WordPress options table
- **Product Settings**: WooCommerce product meta
- **Min Quantity**: Default 25 units
- **Quantity Step**: Default 25 unit increments
- **Volume Break**: Default 75 units
- **Discount Type**: Fixed amount or percentage
- **Discount Amount**: Dollar amount or percentage value

### Pricing Logic

```
Quantity 25-74: Regular price ($19.99)
Quantity 75+: Volume price (Regular - $2.00 = $17.99)
```

### Meta Field Conventions

- **Product Meta**: `_volume_pricing_enabled`, `_volume_pricing_config`
- **Global Options**: `twintack_volume_pricing_enabled`, `twintack_volume_pricing_config`

---

## User Role & Access Patterns

### Grip Workflow Roles (Custom Grips)

- **Art Team** (`grip_art_team`) — Mockup upload; can set `pending_review`
- **Production Team** (`grip_production_team`) — Full status access on team dashboard
- **Customer** — Approve/request changes on own designs when `pending_review`

### Other User Types

- **Regular Customer**: Standard WooCommerce experience
- **Wholesale Customer**: Volume pricing access
- **Affiliate Partner**: Marketing tools access
- **Administrator**: Full system access

---

## Meta Field Naming Conventions

### Grip Design Fields

- **Prefix**: `_grip_` for all grip-related meta
- **Customer Data**: `_grip_customer_*`
- **Design Data**: `_grip_design_*`
- **Workflow Data**: `_grip_artwork_*`
- **Order Data**: `_grip_order_*`, `_grip_final_order_id`

### Volume Pricing Fields

- **Prefix**: `_volume_` for volume pricing meta
- **Product Fields**: `_volume_pricing_*`
- **Global Options**: `twintack_volume_pricing_*`

### General TwinTack Fields

- **Prefix**: `_twintack_` for general theme meta
- **Global Options**: `twintack_*`

---

## Status Management System

### Active Artwork Status Values

| Slug | Label |
|------|-------|
| `artwork_pending` | Mockup Required |
| `pending_review` | Customer Review |
| `customer_requested_changes` | Customer Changes |
| `customer_approved` | Customer Approved |
| `in_production` | In Production |
| `shipped` | Shipped |

### Automatic Transitions (WooCommerce)

- Order **Processing** → `in_production`
- Order **Completed** / **shipped-unpaid** → `shipped`

### Legacy Status Values (migration / display only)

- `approved_for_production` → `in_production` (removed as team step v1.2.4)
- `artwork_approved`, `internal_review` → older records

### Status Display Logic

- **Customer View**: My Custom Grips progress bar and badges via `TTCG_Dashboard`
- **Team View**: Team dashboard filters and status controls
- **Admin View**: Grip Manager meta box (inspection / manual correction)

---

## WooCommerce Integration Patterns

### Product Types

- **Simple Products**: Regular TwinTack products
- **Variable Products**: Products with variations (size, color)
- **Custom Grip Product**: Special handling for grip designs

### Cart & Checkout

- **Cart Metadata**: Store temporary form data
- **Order Processing**: Create posts after deposit payment
- **Order Notes**: Log grip design creation
- **Custom Fields**: Display grip design info in orders
- **Final Purchase**: Links to `_grip_final_order_id`; syncs artwork status

### My Account Integration

- **Canonical endpoint**: `my-custom-grips` (twintack-custom-grips)
- **Legacy endpoint**: `grip-designs` (grip-manager) — redirects when Custom Grips active
- **Dashboard Links**: Role-based navigation
- **Order History**: Show grip design status

---

## Data Validation Rules

### Required Fields Validation

- **Customer Info**: Name, email, team name must not be empty
- **Design Info**: Design type and quantity required
- **Order Link**: Must have valid order ID and item ID
- **Form Data**: Must have valid Gravity Forms entry ID

### Data Sanitization

- **Text Fields**: Use `sanitize_text_field()`
- **Email Fields**: Use `sanitize_email()`
- **URLs**: Use `esc_url_raw()`
- **Numbers**: Use `absint()` for positive integers

---

## Error Handling Patterns

### Form Processing Errors

- **Invalid Data**: Return user-friendly error messages
- **Missing Fields**: Identify specific missing requirements
- **File Upload Issues**: Handle file size/type errors
- **Database Errors**: Log technical details, show generic message

### API Integration Errors

- **External API Failures**: Fallback gracefully
- **Authentication Errors**: Log and notify admin
- **Data Sync Issues**: Queue for retry where possible
- **Rate Limiting**: Implement backoff strategies

---

## Performance Considerations

### Database Queries

- **Avoid N+1 Queries**: Use `WP_Query` with proper meta queries
- **Use Transients**: Cache expensive operations
- **Index Meta Fields**: Consider indexing frequently queried meta
- **Batch Operations**: Process multiple items efficiently

### Caching Strategy

- **Transients**: Use for external API data
- **Object Cache**: Leverage if available
- **Page Cache**: Ensure compatibility with caching plugins
- **Asset Cache**: Optimize CSS/JS loading
